task: Available tasks for this project:
* build:                             Build the server binary
* default:                           List available tasks
* dev:                               Start the map API, web application and public workers
* lint:                              Vet and formatting checks
* setup:                             Install Go tooling and frontend dependencies
* sqlc:                              Regenerate Go database code from SQL
* test:                              Run all Go tests
* assets:validate:test:              Verify the bounded portable model import profile
* build:all:                         Build the API, provisioning tools, and independent Go workers/runtimes
* contracts:buf:                     Lint protobuf contracts with Buf (install Buf separately)
* contracts:buf-breaking:            Check protobuf compatibility against the main branch module
* contracts:openapi:                 Regenerate browser TypeScript types from the OpenAPI contract
* db:backup:                         Create an encrypted-at-rest-ready custom PostgreSQL dump and checksum
* db:down:                           Stop local infrastructure
* db:migrate:                        Apply SQL migrations after the migration preflight
* db:reset:                          Recreate the database volume, migrate, and stop nothing else
* db:restore:test:                   Restore a dump into a temporary database and verify PostGIS/schema integrity
* db:rollback:                       Roll back the most recent migration (production/staging require explicit approval)
* db:status:                         Show migration status
* dev:api:                           Run the Go C4ISR server on the host
* dev:db:                            Start PostgreSQL/PostGIS via Docker Compose
* dev:historical:                    Start the preserved full historical installation explicitly
* dev:web:                           Run the Vite operator UI on the host
* local:backup:                      Create a paired backup after stopping every writer (requires QUIESCED=true)
* local:doctor:                      Diagnose scoped EMAD feature readiness without exposing credentials
* local:restore:test:                Restore the latest paired backup into isolated containers and verify referenced content
* local:setup:                       Install persistent EMAD development infrastructure, identities and real content
* local:setup:historical:            Install preserved historical workers and development identities explicitly
* local:stop:                        Stop the supported development supervisor and workers, preserving database and storage
* map:qualify:sample:                Run an isolated synthetic five-session ten-profile sample (does not qualify MAP-6)
* ops:validate:                      Validate staging Compose, secret mounts, and observability configuration
* scenario:list:                     List available scenarios
* scenario:run:                      Start a scenario by name (NAME=restricted-area-intrusion)
* scenario:runs:                     Show recent scenario runs
* simulation:engine:evaluate:        Compare the same bounded scene in both rendering candidates
* simulation:recordings:build:       Build the independent recording and evaluation worker
* simulation:runtime:build:          Build the independent headless simulation runtime (use -describe to inspect its build)
* simulation:scene:test:             Verify spatial, kinematic and no-GPU scene adapters
* staging:backup:                    Dump the staging database from inside the Compose network
* staging:down:                      Stop staging without deleting persistent volumes
* staging:init:                      Generate ignored staging secret files and the local staging env file
* staging:logs:                      Follow centralized staging logs through Docker
* staging:smoke:                     Exercise the staged API, UI, database readiness, and observability endpoints
* staging:status:                    Show staging service status
* staging:up:                        Build and start the production-shaped local staging stack
* test:browser:integration:          Build the UI and verify public/exercise workflows with PostGIS/S3 (Docker and Chromium required)
* test:e2e:                          Run operator UI browser smoke tests (Chromium required)
* test:integration:                  Run integration tests against real PostgreSQL/PostGIS and S3 (Docker required)
* test:race:                         Run concurrency-sensitive tests with the race detector
* test:unit:                         Run unit tests only
